  "generated_text": "To solve the problem, we start by finding the roots of the quadratic equation \\(x^2 - 3x + 1 = 0\\). The roots can be found using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -3\\), and \\(c = 1\\).\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 4}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the roots are:\n\\[\na = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}, \\quad b = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}\n\\]\n\nWe are asked to find the value of \\(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}}\\). First, we express \\(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}}\\) and \\(\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}}\\) in terms of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}} = a \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3 - \\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}} = b \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3 + \\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the square roots. We rationalize the denominators:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3 - \\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 + \\sqrt{5})}{(3 - \\sqrt{5})(3 + \\sqrt{5})}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 + \\sqrt{5})}{9 - 5}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 + \\sqrt{5})}{4}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3 + \\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 - \\sqrt{5})}{(3 + \\sqrt{5})(3 - \\sqrt{5})}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 - \\sqrt{5})}{9 - 5}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2(3 - \\sqrt{5})}{4}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} = a \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = b \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add these two expressions:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = a \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}} + b \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\nWe know from the properties of the roots of the quadratic equation that \\(a + b = 3\\) and \\(ab = 1\\). We need to simplify the expression further. Notice that:\n\n\\[\na \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}} + b \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity for the sum of roots in a different form. Let's square the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2 = \\left( a \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}} + b \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}} \\right)^2\n\\]\n\nExpanding the square:\n\n\\[\n= a^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} + b^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} + 2ab \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{(3 + \\sqrt{5})(3 - \\sqrt{5})}{4}}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(ab = 1\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n= a^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} + b^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{9 - 5}{4}} = a^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} + b^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{a^2 (3 + \\sqrt{5}) + b^2 (3 - \\sqrt{5})}{2} + 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(a + b = 3\\) and \\(ab = 1\\):\n\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 1 = 9 - 2 = 7\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\na^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} + b^2 \\cdot \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} = \\frac{7(3)}{2} = \\frac{21}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2 = \\frac{21}{2} + 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2\\) must be a perfect square, we simplify:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} \\right)^2 = 8\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{b}} + \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{a}} = \\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]",
